  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Pizzica salentina Southern Italian folk-dance-and-music tradition of the Salento peninsula (southern Puglia), historically tied to the tarantismo ritual-healing tradition where the pizzica dance ostensibly cured tarantism. Characterized by fast 12/8 or 6/8 meter, virtuoso tamburello frame-drum lead, and characteristic call-and-response courtship-and-warrior-dance choreography. Performance contexts include the annual Notte della Taranta festival in Melpignano (founded 1998, now drawing 200,000+ attendees), the canonical Salento-village wedding-and-festival cycle, and (post-2000) the international neo-folk revival circuit. Distinguished from Neapolitan tarantella by pizzica's Salentine regional dialect register and slower tempo-of-instrumental-acceleration arc.",
